# Auto-start Docker When Needed

Before running any command that needs Docker (`docker`, `docker compose`, `supabase start`, `supabase db ...` local commands, `supabase functions serve`, etc.):

1. Check the engine with `docker info`.
2. If it fails, start Docker Desktop without asking:
   `Start-Process "C:\Program Files\Docker\Docker\Docker Desktop.exe"`
3. Poll `docker info` every few seconds until it succeeds (up to ~2 minutes), then continue the task.
4. If it still isn't ready after that, stop and tell the user instead of proceeding.
